course: dictionary
lesson: 5367
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Kite is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, which are its context. «Power lines carry very high voltage, and electricity can jump to a kite string» tells you the kite is the toy on a string, because a string is tied to a toy that flies.
explain: The same word can be an object you buy or count. «Example: 3 kites cost 15 dollars, so one costs 15 / 3 = 5» shows kites as things you can buy, and the sum makes sense only if a kite is an object you can count.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If the sentence still makes sense, you have probably found the right meaning. If not, try another meaning from the dictionary.
fact: A kite is a light toy made of paper, plastic or cloth on a long string that flies in the wind.
fact: A kite can also be a four-sided shape with two pairs of equal sides next to each other, like a diamond that is longer at the bottom.
fact: A kite can also be a bird of prey, like a small hawk.
fact: The phrases «fly a kite» and «as high as a kite» use the toy meaning, and «kite string» is the string you hold.
fact: «Power lines carry very high voltage» so kites and drones are flown in open spaces far from power lines.
exercise: «Power lines carry very high voltage, and electricity can jump to a kite string.» What is a kite in this sentence? | *A light toy flying on a string | A four-sided shape | A bird of prey
exercise: A bird with a hooked beak circles over the field, and Sam says it is a kite. What is a kite here? | A diamond-shaped sign on a wall | *A bird of prey, like a small hawk | A toy made of paper
exercise: «A kite has two pairs of equal sides next to each other.» What is a kite in this sentence? | A bird that hunts | A string for flying | *A four-sided shape
test: «Benjamin Franklin's kite collected electric charge from storm clouds.» What does kite mean in this sentence? | A tall tree | A bird of prey | A cloud in the sky | *A toy kite flown in the wind
test: What does the phrase «as high as a kite» suggest? | Very low, close to the ground | Lost in the rain | *Very high
exam: Which meaning of kite fits «The kite was carried away by the wind»? | A bird that hunts for food | A four-sided shape with equal sides | A cloud that floats high | *A light toy on a string
